From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 12:50:54 +0200
Subject: MIPS: flush the I-cache over the synthesized page handlers

build_clear_page() and build_copy_page() do not compile anything at
build time; they assemble MIPS machine code into .text at boot, through
uasm, into the regions between __clear_page_start/__clear_page_end and
__copy_page_start/__copy_page_end. Those stores go out through the
D-cache. Nothing then tells the I-cache that the instructions it may
already hold for those addresses are stale, and the very next thing
that happens is the CPU fetching and executing them.

arch/mips/mm/tlbex.c, the other place in the architecture that
synthesizes into .text, already invalidates. flush_tlb_handlers() calls
local_flush_icache_range() over handle_tlbl, handle_tlbs, handle_tlbm
and tlbmiss_handler_setup_pgd; each of the three refill-handler builders
flushes the vector it has just written; and traps.c does the same for
the exception-vector copies. page.c is the exception, and
there is no reason for it to be one: synthesized instructions have to
be made visible to the fetch path, and generic architecture code must
not assume any particular CPU's cpu_has_ic_fills_f_dc behaviour makes
that happen by itself.

Add the flush at the end of each builder. The cost is one invalidate
over a few hundred bytes, once, at boot.

The ordering was checked for every cache flavour that calls these
builders, not just the one this was found on: r4k_cache_init(),
octeon_cache_init() and r3k_cache_init() all assign
local_flush_icache_range before calling them, so there is no path that
reaches the new call through a NULL pointer. r4k_cache_init() later
re-points local_flush_icache_range at b5k_instruction_hazard for
BMIPS5000, but only after the builders have run.

A vendor GPL release of Linux 4.9.337 carries the same flush in the
same two places, which is corroboration rather than the argument.

page.c did not include asm/cacheflush.h; it does now.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/arch/mips/mm/page.c b/arch/mips/mm/page.c
index 1df237bd4a72..fa7f9a85f6fe 100644
--- a/arch/mips/mm/page.c
+++ b/arch/mips/mm/page.c
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 #include <linux/proc_fs.h>
 
 #include <asm/bugs.h>
+#include <asm/cacheflush.h>
 #include <asm/cacheops.h>
 #include <asm/cpu-type.h>
 #include <asm/inst.h>
@@ -352,6 +353,9 @@ void build_clear_page(void)
 	for (i = 0; i < (buf - &__clear_page_start); i++)
 		pr_debug("\t.word 0x%08x\n", (&__clear_page_start)[i]);
 	pr_debug("\t.set pop\n");
+
+	local_flush_icache_range((unsigned long)&__clear_page_start,
+				 (unsigned long)&__clear_page_end);
 }
 
 static void build_copy_load(u32 **buf, int reg, int off)
@@ -598,6 +602,9 @@ void build_copy_page(void)
 	for (i = 0; i < (buf - &__copy_page_start); i++)
 		pr_debug("\t.word 0x%08x\n", (&__copy_page_start)[i]);
 	pr_debug("\t.set pop\n");
+
+	local_flush_icache_range((unsigned long)&__copy_page_start,
+				 (unsigned long)&__copy_page_end);
 }
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_SIBYTE_DMA_PAGEOPS
